---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Dmitrii Zhukov The Writer">
  <section class="px-6 pt-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-5">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-4">CH 01</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-6xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-tight md:text-7xl">DZ: The Writer</h1>
        </div>
        <a href="/cv/dmitrii-zhukov-cv.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cv-btn">&#8595; Download CV</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-l text-ink-dim">
        Game writing • Narrative design • Worldbuilding • Lore development • 
        Branching narrative • Narrative Pacing • Character & Dialogue writing • 
        Detective storytelling • Environmental storytelling • Fiction authoring • UI/UX • 
        Cross-functional collaboration
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[250px_1fr]">
        <div class="space-y-6">
        <img
          src="/writer/dz-1.png"
          alt="Dmitrii Zhukov — Writer"
          class="aspect-[3/4] w-full border border-line object-cover"
        />
        
        <aside class="space-y-5 font-mono text-s">
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Status</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· Open to junior & mid game narrative roles</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Toolkit</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· Articy:draft · Twine · Confluence · Notion · Figma · Photoshop · Markdown · MDX · Jira · Git · AI-assisted writing workflows </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Languages</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· English (advanced)<br />· Russian (native)<br />· Ukrainian (advanced)<br />· German (intermediate)<br />· Serbian (beginner)</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Based in</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· Belgrade, Serbia<br />· Open to relocation</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg text-ink-dim">
          <p class="placeholder block"> <span class="font-bold text-violet">[Bio]: </span>My name is <b>Dmitrii Zhukov</b>. I am a game narrative designer 
            and a published fiction writer. I specialize in mystery-driven worlds, atmospheric horror, and psychologically engaging stories. 
            I create worlds, lore, characters, and interactive narratives 
            that invite players 
            to explore, investigate, and uncover mysteries of the plot through the gameplay.<br /><br />My 
            first published 
            novel, <i>Myst</i>, became the foundation for <span class="font-bold text-violet-bright">Static</span>, a game concept that reimagines the 
            story as a third-person psychological action thriller and survival horror 
            experience.</p>
          <p class="placeholder block"><span class="font-bold text-violet">[Career]: </span>Before moving into narrative design, 
            I worked in the fintech industry as a Senior Technical Writer and Product Documentation Manager. I architected and maintained 
            complete documentation ecosystems (knowledge bases, API documentation, release processes, 
            training materials, and internal collaboration platforms). I also acted as a Product Manager 
            and worked closely with Core, QA, Support, and Customer Success teams. I am proficient in 
            organizing complex information, communicating across disciplines, and turning ideas into 
            structured, user-focused experiences.</p>
          <p class="placeholder block"><span class="font-bold text-violet">[Game writing]: </span>Writing has always been at 
            the core of my career (from technical support instructions to full-time technical writers 
            team lead). It has always been my hobby as well: that is why I have invested a lot of 
            time in writing fiction novels. <br /><br />After years of creating documentation for complex software 
            products professionally, I chose to bring together my professional experience with my 
            long-standing commitment to fiction writing and game storytelling. Narrative design and 
            worldbuilding allow me to combine structured thinking, collaboration, and clear 
            communication with a passion for creating immersive worlds and meaningful 
            player experiences.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="rule my-12" />
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl uppercase tracking-tight text-ink">Influences</h2>
      <p class="note mt-1 inline-block">
        
        The stories I invent are shaped by curiosity and observation as much as by fiction as well. 
        Inspiration comes from literature, cinema, video games, music, traveling, education. Visiting 
        XV century castle ruins, listening to a history lecture, or hearing a clever turn of phrase 
        in a song lyric often sparks new ideas: worlds, places, characters, narrative threads. 
        I constantly collect fragments (atmosphere, dialogue pieces, symbolism, plot twists) and 
        then reinterpret them into something new.<br /><br />

        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Games:</span> Bloodborne, Control, Alan Wake, The Last of Us, Hellblade: Senua's Sacrifice, Death Stranding.<br /><br />
        
        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Films:</span> Drive, It Follows, Se7en, Arrival, Memento, Blade Runner 2049.<br /><br />
        
        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Books:</span> One Hundred Years of Solitude, Blood Meridian, Drood, Harry Potter, Ring, The Langoliers.<br /><br />
        
        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Music:</span> Poets of the Fall, STARSET, The Midnight, The National, Oh Hiroshima, Taylor Swift. <br /><br />
        
        Beyond fiction, I draw inspiration from traveling, exploring historic places, museums, architecture, and learning about the people and events 
        that shaped them. Every place and every individual has a story waiting to be uncovered.

      </p>
      
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
